    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0199" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1948v04/pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/11–448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Greece
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-04T18:00:00-05:00">November 4, 1948—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1584. In light of threatened fall coalition govt<anchor n="1" xml:id="d131-f1"/>
                    Dept requests your views possible formation new govt which would command greater
                    popular and international confidence and be able function more effectively. Dept
                    recognizes that reconstitution coalition similar to present, but preferably with
                    new and more effective leadership if available, may be best that can be
                    expected. Dept suggests however desirability consider all other possibilities
                    and extent to which US should and could properly and effectively influence
                    formation govt on different basis. For example do you see any possibility or
                    merit in formation service govt for period emergency with Primin not identified
                    with either major party but with backing both parties or some other coalition
                    that could provide working parliamentary majority? Alternatively, is it possible
                    either Populists or Liberals could, possibly by coalition including splinter
                    parties, form cabinet without the other having parliamentary majority, and would
                    this be desirable meet present <pb facs="0200" n="180" xml:id="pg180"/>
                    situation? Would appreciate your analysis whole political picture without
                    confinement to foregoing suggestions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d131-f1" n="1" xml:id="d131-f1-content">
                <p>Athens, on November 3, had advised of information from the Greek Prime Minister
                    that he would tender his resignation on November 5 (telegram 2218,
                    868.002/11–348).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
